    "q-51403": {
      "dom_id": "step-q51403",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "The population growth of a developing rural area was studied for $25$ years. The following table shows the population $p(t),$ in hundreds, recorded $t$ years after $1990.$\n\n| **$t$** | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p(t)$ | $90$ | $98$ | $116$ | $138$ | $178$ | $220$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nApproximate the population growth rate in the year $2005$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=5.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{p}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{p(t+h)-p(t-h)}{2h}.\n$$\n\n \nWe note that year $2005$ corresponds to $t=15.$ The step size is $h=5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(15) & ≈\\frac{p(15+5)-p(15-5)}{2(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{p(20)-p(10)}{2(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{178-116}{10} \\\\  & =\\frac{62}{10} \\\\  & =6.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the population growth rate in $2005$ was $620$ people per year.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
