    "q-75127": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75127",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14205298/assets/b76466e577343a234b53566b00939a3de312ad4f71106ebf3cbed3bc9d8795ea.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${f}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=8$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=8$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(8) & ≈\\frac{f(8+4)-f(8-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(12)-f(4)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{12-6}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-75127-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "1",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"50\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
